Description: pvr: add the ASTC LDR formats
 BXM-4-64 reports has_astc (common/device_info/bxm-4-64.h), and the texture
 state of Rogue has the 14 two-dimensional ASTC block sizes as
 FORMAT_COMPRESSED values 0 to 13 (csbgen/rogue/texstate.xml). These values
 overlap uncompressed FORMAT values; on cores with tpu_image_state_v2 the
 texture word sets compression mode TPU for every compressed format
 (pvr_arch_pack_tex_state(), IMAGE_WORD1 and STRIDE_IMAGE_WORD1
 tpu_image_state_v2_compression_mode), which selects the compressed format
 table. Copies already handle any block size through pvr_get_raw_copy_format()
 and the block conversions in rogue/pvr_blit.c, as for ETC2 RGBA8 and EAC
 RG11, which also have 128-bit blocks.
 .
 Add the 28 UNORM and SRGB ASTC LDR formats to the format table with sampled
 image support, add the 14 ASTC texture formats to the compressed border
 colour table and report textureCompressionASTC_LDR. ASTC formats are only
 supported, and the feature is only reported, on cores with both astc and
 tpu_image_state_v2; ge7800 and ge8300 have astc without tpu_image_state_v2,
 where the encoding is not described. Linear tiling is not offered for ASTC:
 the stride of a strided texture is given in pixels, and nothing in the
 hardware definitions describes it for blocks that are not a power of two.
 With optimal tiling the formats get sampled image, linear filtering, blit
 source and transfer source and destination, as ETC2. Block-compressed 3D
 images stay unsupported.
 .
 On cores with tpu_border_colour_enhanced the border colour of the ASTC
 formats is stored as U16U16U16U16. On the board, a border colour stored as
 U8U8U8U8 came back as its bytes read as four UNORM16 channels for every
 block size (dEQP-VK.pipeline.monolithic.sampler address_modes
 clamp_to_border, opaque white returned (1, 1, 0, 0)).
 .
 This needs "pvr: lay out twiddled mip levels as power-of-two block grids"
 (patch 0072 in this series) for block sizes that are not a power of two.
 .
 Only for this downstream stack; not intended for upstream submission.
